<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Villalar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1521</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-comuneros">Revolt of the Comuneros</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Villalar was fought on 23 April 1521 near Valladolid, where royalist cavalry routed the army of the Castilian Comuneros. Their leaders Juan de Padilla, Juan Bravo and Francisco Maldonado were beheaded the next day. The defeat ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-comuneros">Revolt of the Comuneros</a>, apart from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a>'s resistance into 1522, and secured the authority of Charles I in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-villalar.jpg" alt="Battle of Villalar" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Manuel Picolo López · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BatallaDeVillalar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
